{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 34, "timestamp": 1785852471, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "NIGHTGLASS — air-gapped dark-vessel detection, end to end"}
[0.070999, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mNIGHTGLASS\u001b[0m  \u001b[2mSAR dark-vessel detection that runs with no route to the internet\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.072578, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m1. One deployment, one AOI. Which one is configuration.\u001b[0m\r\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[1.111288, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m§5 tools\u001b[0m\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n  stac_search     (bbox, start, end)\r\n"]
[1.111312, "o", "  detect_vessels  (scene_id, min_length_m=15.0)\r\n  ais_match       (detections, time_window_min=60, radius_m=500.0)\r\n  doc_search      (query, k=8, filters=None)\r\n  correlate       (bbox, start, end, min_length_m=15.0)\r\n"]
[1.111319, "o", "  draft_intrep    (correlation, context_chunks)\r\n\r\n  AOI  lisbon  -10.5,38.0,-8.5,39.5   AIS aisstream\r\n"]
[1.148316, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m2. An analyst asks. The graph runs, drafts, and stops.\u001b[0m\r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[1.549544, "o", "\u001b[2m$ nightglass-agent ask \"Were there any vessels with no AIS correspondence off Lisbon on 13 June 2026?\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mparse -> plan -> tools -> correlate -> draft_intrep -> HUMAN_GATE\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m(the 14B model is choosing its own tools — ~35 s, live, nothing cached)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.678504, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mNIGHTGLASS agent — lisbon\u001b[0m\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n\u001b[2mthread ng-f4b1dc487f38\u001b[0m\r\nquestion  Were there any vessels with no AIS correspondence off Lisbon on 13 June 2026?\r\n\r\n"]
[34.540502, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mplan\u001b[0m\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n  area of interest: lisbon -10.5,38.0,-8.5,39.5 (from configuration, not the question)\r\n  window: 2026-06-13T00:00 → 2026-06-14T00:00 UTC\r\n  AIS feed: aisstream — demonstration source, not ground truth\r\n  documentary context: none requested\r\n  correlation runs deterministically over the configured AOI after tool use\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mtools the model chose\u001b[0m\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n  1. correlate({\"bbox\": [-10.5, 38, -8.5, 39.5], \"end\": \"2026-06-13T23:59:59Z\", \"min_length_m\": 20,\r\n     \"start\": \"2026-06-13T00:00:00Z\"})\r\n"]
[34.540526, "o", "  2. doc_search({\"query\": \"vessels without AIS correspondence\", \"k\": 5})\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mcorrelation — deterministic, not the model's arithmetic\u001b[0m\r\n-------------------------------------------------------\r\n  1 scene(s), 71 detections, 0 matched, 0 unmatched\r\n"]
[34.540642, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m⏸  HUMAN_GATE — the graph has stopped\u001b[0m\r\n--------------------------------------------\r\n  marking             UNCLASSIFIED // SYNTHETIC // DRAFT — NOT RELEASABLE\r\n  claims              6\r\n  unsupported claims  0\r\n    - A detection with no AIS correspondence is a lead, not a conclusion. Revisit gaps, terrestrial\r\n      coverage limits, transponder failure, class B low-power transponders and vessels not required\r\n      to carry AIS all produce one. The system surfaces candidates; the analyst adjudicates.\r\n    - NO AIS was available for this acquisition window, so none of the 71 detection(s) above has\r\n      been assessed against AIS. They are detections, not dark detections, and nothing here says\r\n      whether any vessel was transmitting. This report carries no correlation finding.\r\n"]
[34.540679, "o", "    - No proportion of unmatched detections is stated in this report. No detections were matched\r\n      against AIS in this correlation. The detector's precision is not validated. Over the Danish\r\n      validation AOI 40% of detections have no AIS correspondence against a published base rate of\r\n      ~5%. The excess is coastal clutter and isolated false alarms, not dark vessels: a\r\n      shoreline-buffer sweep concentrates it near shore, and after duplicate detections of the same\r\n      hull are merged the unmatched fraction rises rather than falls, because it is the matched\r\n      detections that were duplicated. Counts of matched pairs are defensible; a dark-vessel rate is\r\n      not.\r\n"]
[34.540709, "o", "    - DRAFT — NOT RELEASABLE until reviewed and released at the human gate.\r\n\r\n\u001b[2mState is persisted in Postgres. This process can exit; the run cannot\r\nadvance without a human. Inspect it with:\u001b[0m\r\n    nightglass-agent show ng-f4b1dc487f38\r\n    nightglass-agent approve ng-f4b1dc487f38\r\n    nightglass-agent reject ng-f4b1dc487f38 --note \"why\"\r\n"]
[34.884336, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m3. 71 detections, and no verdict. The refusal is the feature.\u001b[0m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[35.285521, "o", "\u001b[2mCounting them all as dark would have read as a spectacular finding. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mcaveat below is assembled from the correlation object, not generated:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[37.680106, "o", "  \u001b[36m - NO AIS was available for this acquisition window, so none of the 71 \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mdetection(s) above has been assessed against AIS. They are detections, \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mnot dark detections, and nothing here says whether any vessel was \u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mtransmitting. This report carries no correlation finding.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[38.083136, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m4. Why a missing transponder is a lead and not a finding.\u001b[0m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[38.484262, "o", "\u001b[2m60 documents embedded locally with bge-m3. The answer is assembled from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mretrieved chunks, and every line carries the chunk it came from.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[42.997621, "o", "Q: when may a vessel lawfully switch its AIS off?\r\n\r\n1. AIS may be switched off if the master believes that continued operation might compromise the safety or security of the ship.\r\n   \u001b[2m[imo-a917-22-ais-guidelines#0013] [imo-a1106-29-ais-operational-use#0015]\u001b[0m\r\n2. The decision to switch off AIS should be recorded in the ship's log and reported to the competent authority if operating in a mandatory ship reporting system.\r\n   \u001b[2m[imo-a1106-29-ais-operational-use#0015]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[43.498538, "o", "\u001b[2mAnd asked something the corpus does not cover, it does not improvise:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[45.799727, "o", "Q: How many dark vessels were detected off Madeira in 2019?\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mNot supported by available sources.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n8 chunk(s) were retrieved but none supported an answer.\r\n"]
[45.903155, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m5. A human releases it — in a different container, from Postgres.\u001b[0m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[46.304361, "o", "\u001b[2mThe process that drafted it has already exited. Nothing is shared but the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mdatabase, so the gate is a real halt rather than a blocked read on stdin.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[48.451437, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mresumed from persisted state — \u001b[32mRELEASED\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n------------------------------------------------\r\n\u001b[2mA different process from the one that drafted it.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nINTREP — lisbon — 2026-08-04\r\nUNCLASSIFIED // SYNTHETIC\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n--------\r\n• The area of interest lisbon was searched between 2026-06-13 00:00 and 2026-06-14 00:00 UTC; the catalogue returned 1 Sentinel-1 granule(s).\r\n    [refs: scene F72E]\r\n"]
[48.704787, "o", "  \u001b[2m^ the marking has lost \"DRAFT — NOT RELEASABLE\". draft_intrep always\r\n    returns releasable=false; this node past the interrupt is the only\r\n    place in the system that can flip it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[48.70658, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m6. The same code, pointed at the AOI that has ground truth.\u001b[0m\r\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[49.107954, "o", "\u001b[2mDenmark publishes free point-level historical AIS — the reason §3.1 made\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mit the validation AOI. Nothing changes here but NIGHTGLASS_AOI.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mOne SQL query over granule S1D_…_BC13, 17 July 2026:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.429912, "o", "  detections                   35\r\n  matched                      21\r\n  dark                         14\r\n  unmatched_fraction           40.0%\r\n  match radius (m)             500.0\r\n  time window (min)            ±11\r\n\r\n  detection                    lat       lon   len m  conf  nearest AIS\r\n  det_00023               56.75648  12.17514      60  1.00  230042000  27 m  Δt +2 s\r\n  det_00017               56.85529  12.38936      80  0.71  319278400  32 m  Δt +33 s\r\n  det_00028               56.69396  11.80493     290  0.96  219115000  40 m  Δt +0 s\r\n"]
[50.469861, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m7. 40% unmatched — and it is still not a dark-vessel rate.\u001b[0m\r\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[50.871136, "o", "\u001b[2mTwo independent guards, over MCP, over the same stdio pipe Claude uses.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[51.999207, "o", "  serverInfo   nightglass 0.1.0   protocol 2025-06-18\r\n"]
[52.069116, "o", "  nightglass_status   aoi=kattegat  ais=dma  ground_truth=True\r\n                      detector_precision_validated=False  ->  dark_rate_quotable=False\r\n"]
[53.978084, "o", "  \u001b[33mThe AIS is ground truth, so that half passes. The detector is not\r\n  precision-validated, so the rate is refused anyway.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[54.381327, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m8. So over Lisbon, ask a second detector instead.\u001b[0m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[55.565259, "o", "ours          71 detections   (nightglass-cfar)\r\nGFW           66 detections   (published layer, same granule)\r\n\r\nboth saw      49   (74% of GFW's, median separation 78 m)\r\nGFW only      17   they found, we did not\r\nours only     22   we found, they did not\r\n\r\nof those 22, how far to the nearest detection we BOTH saw:\r\n  within 200 m   0   (0%)   — too close to be a second vessel\r\n"]
[55.56529, "o", "  median      26064 m\r\n"]
[56.014177, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m9. And none of that had a way out.\u001b[0m\r\n──────────────────────────────────\r\n"]
[56.415213, "o", "\u001b[2m$ docker compose exec api curl -m 5 https://example.com\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[56.547855, "o", "curl: (6) Could not resolve host: example.com\r\n"]
[56.5524, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[32mNot a timeout — an internal network resolves no external name, so no\r\n  packet is ever sent. Every number above came from the far side of that.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
